# User units this spec deploys into ~/.config/systemd/user/ and keeps enabled.
# Read by BOTH assets/scripts/user-units-enable.sh (which enables them) and
# user-units-enable-check.sh (which reports whether they already are), so adding
# a unit is a one-line change in one place.
#
# Only units named here are touched. Enumerating the directory instead would
# enable anything you had dropped in by hand, which is your business.
brave-origin-unlock.service
vivaldi-unlock.service
nextcloud-unlock.service
